## 1. termux/termux-app — GPL-3.0-only

**Upstream:** <https://github.com/termux/termux-app>
**License:** GNU General Public License v3.0 **only** (see
[`terminal-emulator/LICENSE.md`](terminal-emulator/LICENSE.md) and
[`terminal-view/LICENSE.md`](terminal-view/LICENSE.md))
**Vendored as:** the `:terminal-emulator` and `:terminal-view` Gradle modules,
which are copies of the upstream modules of the same name.

This is the single most important attribution in this repository: the entire
terminal — the VT100/xterm emulator, the PTY bridge and the canvas renderer — is
Termux's work, not ours.

| Taken from upstream | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `terminal-emulator/` — `TerminalEmulator`, `TerminalBuffer`, `TerminalRow`, `TerminalSession`, `TerminalColors`, `TextStyle`, `WcWidth`, `ByteQueue`, `KeyHandler`, … (18 Java sources) | Verbatim |
| `terminal-emulator/src/main/cpp/termux.c` — the JNI PTY bridge (`forkpty(3)`, `SIGWINCH`, `waitpid`) | Verbatim |
| `terminal-view/` — `TerminalView`, `TerminalRenderer`, `GestureAndScaleRecognizer`, text-selection cursors, handle drawables (8 Java sources) | Verbatim |

**Changes made by TermAgent** (the only differences from upstream):

* the native bridge is compiled with **CMake** instead of `ndk-build`, and can
  optionally be replaced by a prebuilt `libtermux.so` (see
  [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md));
* modern Gradle configuration (`namespace`, version catalog, Kotlin DSL);
* `res/values/strings.xml` of `:terminal-view` is left as upstream; all app-facing
  strings live in `:app`.

The `terminal-emulator` and `terminal-view` modules remain under **GPL-3.0-only**;
they cannot be relicensed.

